hadow of War</h1>\n    <div class=\"subtitle\">IMF World Economic Outlook Trends 2024–2026 — A synthesis of eight WEO editions tracking global growth, inflation dynamics, and evolving policy priorities amid rising geopolitical uncertainty.</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- KEY METRICS -->\n  <div class=\"metrics-bar\">\n    <div class=\"metric-card\">\n      <div class=\"metric-value\">3.0%</div>\n      <div class=\"metric-label\">Global Growth 2025 (proj.)</div>\n      <div class=\"metric-source\">WEO July 2025</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"metric-card\">\n      <div class=\"metric-value\">3.3%</div>\n      <div class=\"metric-label\">Global Growth 2026 (proj.)</div>\n      <div class=\"metric-source\">WEO January 2026</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"metric-card\">\n      <div class=\"metric-value\">3.2%</div>\n      <div class=\"metric-label\">Global Growth 2027 (proj.)</div>\n      <div class=\"metric-source\">WEO January 2026</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"metric-card\">\n      <div class=\"metric-value\">8</div>\n      <div class=\"metric-label\">WEO Editions Reviewed</div>\n      <div class=\"metric-source\">Jul 2024 – Apr 2026</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"metric-card warning\">\n      <div class=\"metric-value\">Downside</div>\n      <div class=\"metric-label\">Risk Balance — All 8 Editions</div>\n      <div class=\"metric-source\">Consistent finding</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- CONTENT -->\n  <div class=\"content\">\n\n    <!-- GROWTH TRAJECTORY (full width) -->\n    <div class=\"section full-width\">\n      <div class=\"section-label\">Section 1</div>\n      <h2>Global Growth Projections: A Narrow Band of Mediocrity</h2>\n      <div class=\"growth-chart-area\">\n        <table class=\"growth-table\">\n          <thead>\n            <tr>\n              <th>WEO Edition</th>\n              <th>Date</th>\n              <th>2024</th>\n              <th>2025</th>\n              <th>2026</th>\n              <th>2027</th>\n            </tr>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td>Sticky Spot Update</td><td>Jul 2024</td><td class=\"val\">3.2%</td><td class=\"val\">3.3%</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Policy Pivot, Rising Threats</td><td>Oct 2024</td><td class=\"val\">~3.2%</td><td class=\"val\">~3.3%</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Divergent and Uncertain</td><td>Jan 2025</td><td>—</td><td class=\"val\">3.3%</td><td class=\"val\">3.3%</td><td>—</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Critical Juncture</td><td>Apr 2025</td><td>—</td><td class=\"slow\">Slowing</td><td class=\"slow\">Slowing</td><td>—</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Tenuous Resilience</td><td>Jul 2025</td><td>—</td><td class=\"val\">3.0%</td><td class=\"val\">3.1%</td><td>—</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Flux, Prospects Dim</td><td>Oct 2025</td><td>—</td><td class=\"slow\">Slowing</td><td class=\"slow\">Slowing</td><td>—</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Steady amid Divergent Forces</td><td>Jan 2026</td><td>—</td><td class=\"val\">3.3%</td><td class=\"val\">3.2%</td><td class=\"val\">3.2%</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Shadow of War</td><td>Apr 2026</td><td>—</td><td class=\"slow\">Slowing</td><td class=\"slow\">Renewed pressure</td><td>—</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n        <div class=\"growth-band-note\">\n          <div class=\"band\">3.0–3.3%</div>\n          <div class=\"band-text\">Global growth has hovered in this narrow band across all eight editions — well below the <strong>pre-pandemic average of ~3.8%</strong>. The economy isn't collapsing, but it isn't recovering either.</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- DOWNSIDE RISKS -->\n    <div class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"section-label\">Section 2</div>\n      <h2>Dominant Downside Risks</h2>\n\n      <div class=\"risk-callout\">\n        <div class=\"risk-label\">Persistent Finding</div>\n        <div class=\"risk-title\">\"Tilted to the Downside\"</div>\n        <div class=\"risk-sub\">Across all eight WEO editions, the IMF consistently flagged the balance of risks as tilted to the downside.</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <ul class=\"risk-list\">\n        <li>\n          <div class=\"risk-icon\">📉</div>\n          <div class=\"risk-content\">\n            <h4>Trade Policy Escalation</h4>\n            <p>Tariff increases and retaliatory measures, especially from 2025 onward, with front-loading of activity temporarily masking damage.</p>\n          </div>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <div class=\"risk-icon\">🌍</div>\n          <div class=\"risk-content\">\n            <h4>Geopolitical Tensions</h4>\n            <p>Conflicts in the Middle East, broader security concerns, and the war referenced in the April 2026 title.</p>\n          </div>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <div class=\"risk-icon\">💻</div>\n          <div class=\"risk-content\">\n            <h4>Technology Re-evaluation</h4>\n            <p>Risk that elevated expectations around AI and tech investment could face a correction.</p>\n          </div>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <div class=\"risk-icon\">🔥</div>\n          <div class=\"risk-content\">\n            <h4>Persistent Services Inflation</h4>\n            <p>Particularly in the US, where inflation returns to target more gradually than in other advanced economies.</p>\n          </div>\n        </li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- INFLATION DYNAMICS -->\n    <div class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"section-label\">Section 3</div>\n      <h2>Inflation Outlook &amp; Monetary Policy</h2>\n\n      <div class=\"inflation-points\">\n        <div class=\"inflation-point\">\n          <div class=\"dot blue\"></div>\n          <div class=\"ip-text\"><strong>Global headline inflation</strong> is on a declining trajectory, enabling central banks to begin easing — the October 2024 \"policy pivot.\"</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"inflation-point\">\n          <div class=\"dot amber\"></div>\n          <div class=\"ip-text\"><strong>US inflation</strong> is projected to remain above target longer than in peer economies, complicating the Fed's easing path.</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"inflation-point\">\n          <div class=\"dot orange\"></div>\n          <div class=\"ip-text\"><strong>Services inflation</strong> has been particularly sticky across advanced economies, slowing the disinflation process globally.</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"inflation-point\">\n          <div class=\"dot orange\"></div>\n          <div class=\"ip-text\"><strong>Renewed inflationary pressures</strong> emerged by April 2026, linked to rising defense spending and supply chain disruptions from geopolitical conflict.</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- POLICY EVOLUTION -->\n    <div class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"section-label\">Section 4</div>\n      <h2>Evolving Policy Priorities</h2>\n\n      <div class=\"policy-timeline\">\n        <div class=\"policy-step\">\n          <div class=\"policy-period\">Mid-2024</div>\n          <div class=\"policy-desc\">Manage disinflation; begin monetary easing carefully</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"policy-step\">\n          <div class=\"policy-period\">Late 2024</div>\n          <div class=\"policy-desc\">Pivot monetary policy; ensure fiscal sustainability</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"policy-step\">\n          <div class=\"policy-period\">Early 2025</div>\n          <div class=\"policy-desc\">Rebuild fiscal buffers; address demographic and gender gaps</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"policy-step\">\n          <div class=\"policy-period\">Mid-2025</div>\n          <div class=\"policy-desc\">Restore confidence and predictability amid tariff uncertainty</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"policy-step\">\n          <div class=\"policy-period\">Late 2025</div>\n          <div class=\"policy-desc\">Strengthen policy frameworks; cautious industrial policy</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"policy-step\">\n          <div class=\"policy-period\">Early 2026</div>\n          <div class=\"policy-desc\">Agile policy; manage defense-spending trade-offs; lay foundations for recovery</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- SPECIAL THEMES -->\n    <div class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"section-label\">Section 5</div>\n      <h2>Special Themes Across WEO Editions</h2>\n\n      <div class=\"themes-grid\">\n        <div class=\"theme-card\">\n          <h4>Monetary Policy &amp; Disinflation</h4>\n          <p>Role of central bank credibility and coordination in achieving soft landings.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"theme-card\">\n          <h4>Industrial Policy</h4>\n          <p>Effectiveness and fiscal cost of state-directed economic interventions.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"theme-card\">\n          <h4>Social Acceptability of Reforms</h4>\n          <p>Political economy of structural reform — who bears adjustment costs.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"theme-card\">\n          <h4>Demographics &amp; Labor Markets</h4>\n          <p>Policies for aging populations, gender disparities, and migrant skill alignment.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- FOOTER -->\n  <div class=\"footer\">\n    <div class=\"source\">Source: IMF World Economic Outlook (WEO), July 2024 – April 2026 | 8 editions reviewed</div>\n    <div>IMF–World Bank Annual Meetings Research Symposium | April 2026</div>\n  </div>\n\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n", "numLines": 650, "startLine": 1, "totalLines": 650}}

